      }
    },
    "A benzofuran analogue of MDA that acts as a serotonin-predominant monoamine releasing agent. Releases serotonin, dopamine, and norepinephrine with strong SERT selectivity. Also acts as a 5-HT2B agonist, which raises cardiovascular safety concerns with repeated use. Produces empathogenic effects similar to MDMA with a longer duration of action." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "MDA 的苯并呋喃类似物,作为以血清素为主的单胺释放剂。通过强 SERT 选择性释放血清素、多巴胺和去甲肾上腺素。同时也是 5-HT2B 激动剂,反复使用引起心血管安全顾虑。产生类似 MDMA 的共感效应,但作用时间更长。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "MDA 的苯並呋喃類似物,作為以血清素為主的單胺釋放劑。透過強 SERT 選擇性釋放血清素、多巴胺和去甲腎上腺素。同時也是 5-HT2B 激動劑,反覆使用引起心血管安全顧慮。產生類似 MDMA 的共感效應,但作用時間更長。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A benzofuran analogue that releases serotonin, dopamine, and norepinephrine via transporter reversal. Acts as an agonist at 5-HT2B receptors. Produces empathogenic and mildly psychedelic effects with a profile between MDMA and MDA." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "苯并呋喃类似物,通过转运体反转释放血清素、多巴胺和去甲肾上腺素。作为 5-HT2B 受体激动剂。产生介于 MDMA 与 MDA 之间的共感和轻度致幻效应。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "苯並呋喃類似物,透過轉運體反轉釋放血清素、多巴胺和去甲腎上腺素。作為 5-HT2B 受體激動劑。產生介於 MDMA 與 MDA 之間的共感和輕度致幻效應。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A change of scenery — even moving to a different room — can shift your headspace." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "换个环境 — 即使只是换到另一个房间 — 可以改变心境。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "換個環境 — 即使只是換到另一個房間 — 可以改變心境。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A complete backup you can restore into Piru" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "可恢复到 Piru 的完整备份"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "可還原至 Piru 的完整備份"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A cool, dark room helps with headaches and overstimulation." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "凉爽、昏暗的房间有助于缓解头痛和过度刺激。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "涼爽、昏暗的房間有助於緩解頭痛和過度刺激。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A custom substance named \"%@\" already exists." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "已存在名为 \"%@\" 的自定义物质。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "已存在名為 \"%@\" 的自訂物質。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A dipeptide nootropic structurally related to racetams but with distinct pharmacology. Modulates AMPA and NMDA glutamate receptors, enhancing long-term potentiation (LTP) and synaptic plasticity. Increases expression of brain-derived neurotrophic factor (BDNF) and nerve growth factor (NGF). Active at much lower doses than piracetam, suggesting additional mechanisms beyond glutamatergic modulation." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "结构与吡拉西坦类相关但药理学独特的二肽益智剂。调节 AMPA 和 NMDA 谷氨酸受体,增强长时程增强 (LTP) 和突触可塑性。增加脑源性神经营养因子 (BDNF) 和神经生长因子 (NGF) 的表达。在远低于吡拉西坦的剂量下即有效,提示存在谷氨酸能调节之外的其他机制。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "結構與吡拉西坦類相關但藥理學獨特的二肽益智劑。調節 AMPA 和 NMDA 麩胺酸受體,增強長時程增強 (LTP) 和突觸可塑性。增加腦源性神經滋養因子 (BDNF) 和神經生長因子 (NGF) 的表達。在遠低於吡拉西坦的劑量下即有效,提示存在麩胺酸能調節之外的其他機制。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A few things to set up before you start." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "开始之前需要先设置几项内容。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "開始之前需要先設定幾項內容。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A fictional drug from a 1997 TV satire on media drug panics — “Cake” isn’t real, and nothing below is either. It supposedly overstimulates “Shatner’s Bassoon,” the part of the brain that governs time. Made in Prague." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "出自 1997 年一部讽刺媒体毒品恐慌的电视节目的虚构药物——“Cake”并不存在，下面的内容也都是假的。据说它会过度刺激控制时间感的大脑区域“夏特纳的巴松管（Shatner’s Bassoon）”。产自布拉格。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "出自 1997 年一部諷刺媒體毒品恐慌的電視節目的虛構藥物——「Cake」並不存在，下面的內容也都是假的。據說它會過度刺激控制時間感的大腦區域「夏特納的巴松管（Shatner’s Bassoon）」。產自布拉格。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A notification repeats daily at this time." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "每天此时重复发送通知。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "每天此時重複傳送通知。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A passphrase is required." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "需要口令。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "需要通行碼。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A passphrase-protected .piruenc file" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "由口令保护的 .piruenc 文件"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "由通行密語保護的 .piruenc 檔案"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A PDF summary to share with a clinician" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "可与医生分享的 PDF 摘要"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "可與醫師分享的 PDF 摘要"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A pharmacologically inactive prodrug cleaved in red blood cells to release dextroamphetamine and L-lysine. The dextroamphetamine then acts as a monoamine releasing agent via DAT, NET, SERT reversal and TAAR1 activation. The prodrug formulation provides controlled, gradual release of active drug, reducing abuse potential and producing smoother pharmacokinetics compared to immediate-release amphetamine." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "在红细胞中被裂解释放右苯丙胺和 L-赖氨酸的药理学无活性前药。释放的右苯丙胺通过 DAT、NET、SERT 反转和 TAAR1 激活作为单胺释放剂。前药剂型提供受控、渐进的活性药物释放,降低滥用潜力,并比立即释放型苯丙胺产生更平滑的药代动力学。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "在紅血球中被裂解釋放右苯丙胺和 L-離胺酸的藥理學無活性前藥。釋放的右苯丙胺透過 DAT、NET、SERT 反轉和 TAAR1 激活作為單胺釋放劑。前藥劑型提供受控、漸進的活性藥物釋放,降低濫用潛力,並比立即釋放型苯丙胺產生更平滑的藥動學。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A phospholipid that serves as a precursor to acetylcholine. Crosses the blood-brain barrier and increases acetylcholine synthesis and release in the brain. Also provides glycerophosphate for membrane phospholipid synthesis. Enhances cholinergic neurotransmission, which is involved in memory formation, attention, and learning." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为乙酰胆碱前体的磷脂。穿过血脑屏障,增加脑内乙酰胆碱的合成和释放。也提供甘油磷酸用于膜磷脂合成。增强胆碱能神经传递,后者参与记忆形成、注意力和学习。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為乙醯膽鹼前體的磷脂。穿過血腦屏障,增加腦內乙醯膽鹼的合成和釋放。也提供甘油磷酸用於膜磷脂合成。增強膽鹼能神經傳遞,後者參與記憶形成、注意力和學習。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A Piru or PsychonautWiki JSON file" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Piru 或 PsychonautWiki 的 JSON 文件"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Piru 或 PsychonautWiki 的 JSON 檔案"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A positional isomer of Δ9-THC with the double bond at the 8th carbon position. Acts as a partial agonist at CB1 receptors with approximately 50-75% the potency of Δ9-THC. Produces similar but milder psychoactive effects including euphoria, relaxation, and altered perception." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Δ9-THC 的位置异构体,双键位于第 8 位碳。作为 CB1 受体部分激动剂,强度约为 Δ9-THC 的 50-75%。产生类似但更温和的精神活性效应,包括欣快、放松和感知改变。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Δ9-THC 的位置異構物,雙鍵位於第 8 位碳。作為 CB1 受體部分激動劑,強度約為 Δ9-THC 的 50-75%。產生類似但更溫和的精神活性效應,包括欣快、放鬆和感知改變。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A prodrug converted to GHB via alcohol dehydrogenase and aldehyde dehydrogenase. Once converted, acts on GHB and GABA-B receptors. Onset and duration depend on hepatic enzyme activity. Co-administration with ethanol competitively inhibits conversion, unpredictably altering pharmacokinetics." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "通过醇脱氢酶和醛脱氢酶转化为 GHB 的前药。转化后作用于 GHB 和 GABA-B 受体。起效和持续时间取决于肝酶活性。与乙醇共同给药会竞争性抑制转化,不可预测地改变药代动力学。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "透過醇脫氫酶和醛脫氫酶轉化為 GHB 的前藥。轉化後作用於 GHB 和 GABA-B 受體。起效和持續時間取決於肝酶活性。與乙醇共同給藥會競爭性抑制轉化,不可預測地改變藥動學。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A prodrug rapidly dephosphorylated to psilocin by alkaline phosphatase. Psilocin acts as an agonist at serotonin 5-HT2A receptors (primary psychedelic target), with additional activity at 5-HT2C, 5-HT1A, and other serotonin subtypes. 5-HT2A activation on cortical pyramidal neurons increases glutamate release and enhances connectivity between brain networks that are normally segregated, producing altered perception and consciousness." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "由碱性磷酸酶迅速去磷酸化为裸盖菇素的前药。裸盖菇素作为血清素 5-HT2A 受体(主要致幻靶点)的激动剂,同时对 5-HT2C、5-HT1A 等血清素亚型也有活性。皮质锥体神经元上的 5-HT2A 激活会增加谷氨酸释放,增强通常分离的脑网络之间的连接,产生感知和意识的改变。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "由鹼性磷酸酶迅速去磷酸化為裸蓋菇素的前藥。裸蓋菇素作為血清素 5-HT2A 受體(主要致幻靶點)的激動劑,同時對 5-HT2C、5-HT1A 等血清素亞型也有活性。皮質錐體神經元上的 5-HT2A 激活會增加麩胺酸釋放,增強通常分離的腦網路之間的連結,產生感知和意識的改變。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A prodrug that is metabolized to morphine by the cytochrome P450 enzyme CYP2D6. Codeine itself has very weak affinity for μ-opioid receptors; its analgesic and antitussive effects depend on conversion to morphine. Genetic polymorphisms in CYP2D6 significantly affect efficacy — poor metabolizers get little benefit, while ultra-rapid metabolizers may experience dangerous opioid levels." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "由细胞色素 P450 酶 CYP2D6 代谢为吗啡的前药。可待因本身对 μ-阿片受体亲和力很弱;其镇痛和止咳效应依赖于转化为吗啡。CYP2D6 的基因多态性显著影响疗效 — 慢代谢者获益甚少,而超快代谢者可能出现危险的阿片水平。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "由細胞色素 P450 酶 CYP2D6 代謝為嗎啡的前藥。可待因本身對 μ-阿片受體親和力很弱;其鎮痛和止咳效應依賴於轉化為嗎啡。CYP2D6 的基因多型性顯著影響療效 — 慢代謝者獲益甚少,而超快代謝者可能出現危險的阿片水平。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A prodrug that is partially metabolized to meprobamate, which acts as a positive allosteric modulator at GABA-A receptors. The parent compound may also directly modulate GABA-A receptors and other targets. Produces muscle relaxation, sedation, and anxiolysis. The meprobamate metabolite has a long half-life and contributes to dependence potential." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "部分代谢为美普巴马的前药,后者作为 GABA-A 受体的正向变构调节剂。母体化合物也可能直接调节 GABA-A 受体和其他靶点。产生肌肉松弛、镇静和抗焦虑作用。美普巴马代谢物半衰期较长,助长依赖性潜力。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "部分代謝為美普巴馬的前藥,後者作為 GABA-A 受體的正向變構調節劑。母體化合物也可能直接調節 GABA-A 受體和其他靶點。產生肌肉鬆弛、鎮靜和抗焦慮作用。美普巴馬代謝物半衰期較長,助長依賴性潛力。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A prodrug that is rapidly converted to GHB (gamma-hydroxybutyrate) by peripheral lactonases. Once converted, acts as an agonist at GHB receptors and GABA-B receptors. Has faster onset than GHB due to rapid absorption and conversion. Carries the same steep dose-response curve and overdose risks as GHB." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "由外周内酯酶迅速转化为 GHB(γ-羟基丁酸)的前药。转化后作为 GHB 受体和 GABA-B 受体的激动剂。由于吸收和转化快速,起效比 GHB 更快。具有与 GHB 相同的陡峭剂量-反应曲线和过量风险。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "由外周內酯酶迅速轉化為 GHB(γ-羥基丁酸)的前藥。轉化後作為 GHB 受體和 GABA-B 受體的激動劑。由於吸收和轉化快速,起效比 GHB 更快。具有與 GHB 相同的陡峭劑量-反應曲線和過量風險。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A pyrrolidine cathinone that potently blocks the dopamine and norepinephrine transporters (DAT/NET) without releasing monoamines and with little serotonergic activity. The strong, long-lasting rise in dopamine and norepinephrine is intensely stimulating and carries a high risk of compulsive redosing." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "一种吡咯烷类卡西酮,强效阻断多巴胺和去甲肾上腺素转运体(DAT/NET),不释放单胺,血清素活性很弱。多巴胺和去甲肾上腺素强烈而持久地升高,带来强烈兴奋,并伴有很高的强迫性反复用药风险。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "一種吡咯烷類卡西酮,強效阻斷多巴胺和正腎上腺素轉運體(DAT/NET),不釋放單胺,血清素活性很弱。多巴胺和正腎上腺素強烈而持久地升高,帶來強烈興奮,並伴有很高的強迫性反覆用藥風險。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A structural derivative of carbamazepine that blocks voltage-gated sodium channels in their inactivated state. Rapidly converted to its active metabolite licarbazepine (MHD). Compared to carbamazepine, has a more favorable side effect profile and fewer drug interactions due to reduced hepatic enzyme induction." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "卡马西平的结构衍生物,在失活态阻滞电压门控钠通道。迅速转化为活性代谢物 licarbazepine (MHD)。相较于卡马西平,因肝酶诱导减少,副作用谱更佳,药物相互作用较少。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "卡馬西平的結構衍生物,在失活態阻滯電壓門控鈉通道。迅速轉化為活性代謝物 licarbazepine (MHD)。相較於卡馬西平,因肝酶誘導減少,副作用譜更佳,藥物相互作用較少。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A structurally unique non-nitrogenous terpenoid that acts as a highly potent and selective agonist at κ-opioid receptors (KOR). Unlike virtually all other psychoactive compounds, has no significant activity at serotonin 5-HT2A receptors. KOR activation in the claustrum and prefrontal cortex produces intensely dissociative and hallucinatory effects. The most potent naturally occurring psychoactive compound by weight." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "结构独特的非氮萜类化合物,作为高效且选择性的 κ-阿片受体 (KOR) 激动剂。与几乎所有其他精神活性化合物不同,对血清素 5-HT2A 受体无显著活性。屏状核和前额叶皮质中的 KOR 激活产生强烈的解离和致幻效应。按重量计算,是最强效的天然存在的精神活性化合物。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "結構獨特的非氮萜類化合物,作為高效且選擇性的 κ-阿片受體 (KOR) 激動劑。與幾乎所有其他精神活性化合物不同,對血清素 5-HT2A 受體無顯著活性。屏狀核和前額葉皮質中的 KOR 激活產生強烈的解離和致幻效應。按重量計算,是最強效的天然存在的精神活性化合物。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A synthetic phenyl derivative of GABA that crosses the blood-brain barrier, unlike GABA itself. Primarily acts as a GABA-B receptor agonist, producing anxiolytic and sedative effects. Also binds the α2δ subunit of voltage-gated calcium channels, similar to gabapentin, reducing excitatory neurotransmitter release. At high doses, may weakly activate GABA-A receptors." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "可穿过血脑屏障的 GABA 合成苯基衍生物(与 GABA 本身不同)。主要作为 GABA-B 受体激动剂,产生抗焦虑和镇静作用。也与电压门控钙通道的 α2δ 亚单位结合(类似加巴喷丁),减少兴奋性神经递质释放。高剂量下可能弱激活 GABA-A 受体。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "可穿過血腦屏障的 GABA 合成苯基衍生物(與 GABA 本身不同)。主要作為 GABA-B 受體激動劑,產生抗焦慮和鎮靜作用。也與電壓門控鈣通道的 α2δ 亞單位結合(類似加巴噴丁),減少興奮性神經傳導物質釋放。高劑量下可能弱激活 GABA-A 受體。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A warm bath can ease the achy, restless feeling." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "温水浴可以缓解酸痛和不安感。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "溫水浴可以緩解痠痛和不安感。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A warm shower or light stretching helps your muscles release." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "温水淋浴或轻度拉伸有助于肌肉放松。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "溫水淋浴或輕度拉伸有助於肌肉放鬆。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A β-keto amphetamine that enters dopamine, norepinephrine, and serotonin nerve terminals through their transporters (DAT/NET/SERT) and reverses them, releasing all three monoamines. The dopamine-to-serotonin release ratio sets the character — balanced (e.g. mephedrone) is entactogenic-stimulant, dopamine-dominant is more purely stimulating." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "一种β-酮苯丙胺,经转运体(DAT/NET/SERT)进入多巴胺、去甲肾上腺素和血清素神经末梢并使其反向转运,释放这三种单胺。多巴胺与血清素的释放比例决定其特性——比例均衡(如甲卡西酮)偏向移情兴奋,多巴胺占主导则更偏纯粹兴奋。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "一種β-酮苯丙胺,經轉運體(DAT/NET/SERT)進入多巴胺、正腎上腺素和血清素神經末梢並使其反向轉運,釋放這三種單胺。多巴胺與血清素的釋放比例決定其特性——比例均衡(如甲卡西酮)偏向移情興奮,多巴胺佔主導則更偏純粹興奮。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "About" : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "关于"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "關於"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Absolutely do not drive or operate machinery." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "绝对不要驾驶或操作机器。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "絕對不要駕駛或操作機器。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acid, nausea, and gut motility." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "胃酸、恶心与胃肠动力。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "胃酸、噁心與胃腸動力。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acil Yardim" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Acil Yardim"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Acil Yardim"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Action" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作用"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作用"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Activates melatonin MT1 and MT2 receptors in the suprachiasmatic nucleus (SCN), the master circadian clock. MT1 activation suppresses SCN neuronal firing, promoting sleep onset. MT2 activation shifts the circadian phase, entraining the sleep-wake cycle. Endogenous melatonin is produced by the pineal gland in response to darkness; exogenous melatonin mimics this signal." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "激活视交叉上核 (SCN, 主昼夜节律时钟) 中的褪黑素 MT1 和 MT2 受体。MT1 激活抑制 SCN 神经元放电,促进入睡。MT2 激活转换昼夜相位,牵引睡眠-觉醒周期。内源性褪黑素由松果体响应黑暗而产生;外源性褪黑素模拟此信号。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "激活視交叉上核 (SCN, 主晝夜節律時鐘) 中的褪黑素 MT1 和 MT2 受體。MT1 激活抑制 SCN 神經元放電,促進入睡。MT2 激活轉換晝夜相位,牽引睡眠-覺醒週期。內源性褪黑素由松果體響應黑暗而產生;外源性褪黑素模擬此訊號。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Activates presynaptic α2-adrenergic receptors in the locus coeruleus and brainstem, reducing norepinephrine release and sympathetic outflow. Decreases heart rate, blood pressure, and peripheral vascular resistance. In opioid and alcohol withdrawal, reduces the noradrenergic hyperactivity responsible for anxiety, tachycardia, and diaphoresis. Also has activity at imidazoline I1 receptors." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "激活蓝斑和脑干中的突触前 α2-肾上腺素受体,减少去甲肾上腺素释放和交感输出。降低心率、血压和外周血管阻力。在阿片和酒精戒断中,减少导致焦虑、心动过速和出汗的去甲肾上腺素能过度活跃。也对咪唑啉 I1 受体有活性。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "激活藍斑和腦幹中的突觸前 α2-腎上腺素受體,減少去甲腎上腺素釋放和交感輸出。降低心率、血壓和外周血管阻力。在阿片和酒精戒斷中,減少導致焦慮、心動過速和出汗的去甲腎上腺素能過度活躍。也對咪唑啉 I1 受體有活性。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "active" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "有活性"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "有活性"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Active" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "活跃"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "活躍"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Active dose details" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "活性剂量详情"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "活性劑量詳情"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Active in microgram (µg) quantities — 1/1000th of a milligram. Volumetric dosing is required at all times for safe and accurate measurement. Never attempt to measure doses by eye or with standard scales." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "微克(µg)量级即有效 — 即一毫克的千分之一。任何时候都必须使用容积式给药以确保安全准确的测量。绝不要靠目测或用普通秤来称量剂量。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "微克(µg)量級即有效 — 即一毫克的千分之一。任何時候都必須使用容積式給藥以確保安全準確的測量。絕不要靠目測或用普通秤來秤量劑量。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Activity" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "活动"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "活動"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as a competitive antagonist at μ-opioid receptors (MOR), with lower affinity for κ and δ receptors. Rapidly displaces opioid agonists from MOR, reversing respiratory depression, sedation, and analgesia. Has poor oral bioavailability due to extensive first-pass metabolism, necessitating parenteral or intranasal administration. Short duration of action (30–90 minutes) may require repeat dosing for long-acting opioids." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为 μ-阿片受体 (MOR) 的竞争性拮抗剂,对 κ 和 δ 受体亲和力较低。迅速将阿片激动剂从 MOR 置换,逆转呼吸抑制、镇静和镇痛。由于广泛的首过代谢,口服生物利用度差,需要肠外或鼻内给药。作用时间短 (30–90 分钟),对长效阿片可能需要重复给药。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為 μ-阿片受體 (MOR) 的競爭性拮抗劑,對 κ 和 δ 受體親和力較低。迅速將阿片激動劑從 MOR 置換,逆轉呼吸抑制、鎮靜和鎮痛。由於廣泛的首過代謝,口服生物利用度差,需要腸外或鼻內給藥。作用時間短 (30–90 分鐘),對長效阿片可能需要重複給藥。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as a competitive antagonist at μ, κ, and δ-opioid receptors with good oral bioavailability and long duration of action (24–72 hours). At standard doses (50 mg), blocks the euphoric effects of exogenous opioids. Also used for alcohol use disorder, where it reduces alcohol-induced dopamine release and craving through opioid system modulation." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为 μ、κ 和 δ-阿片受体的竞争性拮抗剂,具良好口服生物利用度和长作用时间 (24–72 小时)。标准剂量 (50 mg) 下阻断外源性阿片的欣快效应。也用于酒精使用障碍,通过调节阿片系统减少酒精诱导的多巴胺释放和渴求。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為 μ、κ 和 δ-阿片受體的競爭性拮抗劑,具良好口服生物利用度和長作用時間 (24–72 小時)。標準劑量 (50 mg) 下阻斷外源性阿片的欣快效應。也用於酒精使用障礙,透過調節阿片系統減少酒精誘導的多巴胺釋放和渴求。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as a competitive antagonist at μ, κ, and δ-opioid receptors, with highest affinity for μ-opioid receptors. Displaces opioid agonists from receptors, reversing opioid-induced respiratory depression, sedation, and analgesia. Used for opioid overdose reversal and maintenance treatment of opioid and alcohol use disorders." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为 μ、κ 和 δ-阿片受体的竞争性拮抗剂,对 μ-阿片受体亲和力最高。将阿片激动剂从受体上置换,逆转阿片诱导的呼吸抑制、镇静和镇痛。用于阿片过量逆转及阿片和酒精使用障碍的维持治疗。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為 μ、κ 和 δ-阿片受體的競爭性拮抗劑,對 μ-阿片受體親和力最高。將阿片激動劑從受體上置換,逆轉阿片誘導的呼吸抑制、鎮靜和鎮痛。用於阿片過量逆轉及阿片和酒精使用障礙的維持治療。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as a full agonist at μ-opioid receptors (MOR), G-protein coupled receptors distributed throughout the central and peripheral nervous system. MOR activation inhibits adenylyl cyclase, opens inwardly rectifying potassium channels, and closes voltage-gated calcium channels, reducing neuronal excitability and neurotransmitter release. Produces analgesia, euphoria, respiratory depression, and decreased gastrointestinal motility." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为 μ-阿片受体 (MOR) 的完全激动剂,这是分布于中枢和外周神经系统的 G 蛋白偶联受体。MOR 激活抑制腺苷酸环化酶,开放内向整流钾通道,关闭电压门控钙通道,降低神经元兴奋性和神经递质释放。产生镇痛、欣快、呼吸抑制和胃肠动力降低。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為 μ-阿片受體 (MOR) 的完全激動劑,這是分布於中樞和外周神經系統的 G 蛋白偶聯受體。MOR 激活抑制腺苷酸環化酶,開放內向整流鉀通道,關閉電壓門控鈣通道,降低神經元興奮性和神經傳導物質釋放。產生鎮痛、欣快、呼吸抑制和胃腸動力降低。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as a full agonist at μ-opioid receptors with additional NMDA receptor antagonist activity. The NMDA antagonism may reduce opioid tolerance development and contribute to analgesic efficacy in neuropathic pain. Has a very long and variable half-life (15–60 hours), providing sustained opioid receptor occupancy that suppresses withdrawal and craving. Also weakly inhibits serotonin and norepinephrine reuptake." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为 μ-阿片受体的完全激动剂,并具有附加的 NMDA 受体拮抗活性。NMDA 拮抗作用可能减少阿片耐受发展,并对神经病理性疼痛的镇痛疗效有贡献。半衰期非常长且不固定 (15–60 小时),提供持续的阿片受体占用,抑制戒断和渴求。也弱抑制血清素和去甲肾上腺素的再摄取。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為 μ-阿片受體的完全激動劑,並具有附加的 NMDA 受體拮抗活性。NMDA 拮抗作用可能減少阿片耐受發展,並對神經病理性疼痛的鎮痛療效有貢獻。半衰期非常長且不固定 (15–60 小時),提供持續的阿片受體佔用,抑制戒斷和渴求。也弱抑制血清素和去甲腎上腺素的再攝取。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as a high-affinity partial agonist at μ-opioid receptors (MOR), producing submaximal receptor activation even at full occupancy. This creates a ceiling effect for respiratory depression while providing effective analgesia and opioid withdrawal relief. Simultaneously antagonizes κ-opioid receptors (KOR), which may contribute to antidepressant and anti-dysphoric effects. Slow receptor dissociation contributes to its long duration of action." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为 μ-阿片受体 (MOR) 的高亲和力部分激动剂,即使完全占用也产生亚最大受体激活。这为呼吸抑制创造了天花板效应,同时提供有效的镇痛和阿片戒断缓解。同时拮抗 κ-阿片受体 (KOR),可能对抗抑郁和抗烦躁效应有贡献。受体解离缓慢助长其长作用时间。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為 μ-阿片受體 (MOR) 的高親和力部分激動劑,即使完全佔用也產生亞最大受體激活。這為呼吸抑制創造了天花板效應,同時提供有效的鎮痛和阿片戒斷緩解。同時拮抗 κ-阿片受體 (KOR),可能對抗鬱和抗煩躁效應有貢獻。受體解離緩慢助長其長作用時間。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as a low-affinity, uncompetitive NMDA receptor antagonist with rapid on/off kinetics. At therapeutic concentrations, preferentially blocks pathologically activated (tonically open) NMDA receptors while preserving normal phasic (synaptic) NMDA signaling. This selectivity reduces excitotoxic neuronal damage in Alzheimer's disease without producing the dissociative effects seen with higher-affinity NMDA antagonists like ketamine." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为具快速开关动力学的低亲和力非竞争性 NMDA 受体拮抗剂。在治疗浓度下,优先阻断病理性激活(持续开放)的 NMDA 受体,同时保留正常的相位性(突触)NMDA 信号传导。这种选择性减少阿尔茨海默病中的兴奋性毒性神经元损伤,且不产生氯胺酮等高亲和力 NMDA 拮抗剂所见的解离效应。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為具快速開關動力學的低親和力非競爭性 NMDA 受體拮抗劑。在治療濃度下,優先阻斷病理性激活(持續開放)的 NMDA 受體,同時保留正常的相位性(突觸)NMDA 訊號傳導。這種選擇性減少阿茲海默病中的興奮性毒性神經元損傷,且不產生氯胺酮等高親和力 NMDA 拮抗劑所見的解離效應。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as a non-competitive antagonist at the NMDA glutamate receptor by binding within the ion channel pore (use-dependent blockade). Produces dissociative anesthesia at higher doses and rapid antidepressant effects at sub-anesthetic doses. The antidepressant mechanism involves enhanced AMPA receptor signaling, increased brain-derived neurotrophic factor (BDNF) release, and activation of the mTOR signaling pathway, promoting rapid synaptic plasticity." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "通过结合于离子通道孔内(使用依赖性阻断)作为 NMDA 谷氨酸受体的非竞争性拮抗剂。在较高剂量下产生解离性麻醉,在亚麻醉剂量下产生快速抗抑郁效应。抗抑郁机制涉及 AMPA 受体信号增强、脑源性神经营养因子 (BDNF) 释放增加,以及 mTOR 信号通路激活,促进快速突触可塑性。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "透過結合於離子通道孔內(使用依賴性阻斷)作為 NMDA 麩胺酸受體的非競爭性拮抗劑。在較高劑量下產生解離性麻醉,在亞麻醉劑量下產生快速抗鬱效應。抗鬱機制涉及 AMPA 受體訊號增強、腦源性神經滋養因子 (BDNF) 釋放增加,以及 mTOR 訊號通路激活,促進快速突觸可塑性。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as a partial agonist at cannabinoid CB1 receptors in the central nervous system, mimicking the endogenous cannabinoid anandamide. CB1 receptors are presynaptic on GABAergic and glutamatergic neurons; their activation reduces neurotransmitter release via retrograde signaling. This modulates synaptic plasticity, pain perception, appetite, memory consolidation, and motor coordination. Also weakly activates CB2 receptors." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为中枢神经系统中大麻素 CB1 受体的部分激动剂,模拟内源性大麻素花生四烯酸乙醇胺。CB1 受体位于 GABA 能和谷氨酸能神经元的突触前;其激活通过逆向信号传导减少神经递质释放。这调节突触可塑性、痛觉、食欲、记忆固化和运动协调。也弱激活 CB2 受体。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為中樞神經系統中大麻素 CB1 受體的部分激動劑,模擬內源性大麻素花生四烯酸乙醇胺。CB1 受體位於 GABA 能和麩胺酸能神經元的突觸前;其激活透過逆向訊號傳導減少神經傳導物質釋放。這調節突觸可塑性、痛覺、食慾、記憶固化和運動協調。也弱激活 CB2 受體。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as a partial agonist at cannabinoid CB1 receptors in the central nervous system, mimicking the endogenous cannabinoid anandamide. Reduces neurotransmitter release via retrograde signaling at presynaptic CB1 receptors on GABAergic and glutamatergic neurons." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为中枢神经系统中大麻素 CB1 受体的部分激动剂,模拟内源性大麻素花生四烯酸乙醇胺。通过 GABA 能和谷氨酸能神经元突触前 CB1 受体的逆向信号传导减少神经递质释放。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為中樞神經系統中大麻素 CB1 受體的部分激動劑,模擬內源性大麻素花生四烯酸乙醇胺。透過 GABA 能和麩胺酸能神經元突觸前 CB1 受體的逆向訊號傳導減少神經傳導物質釋放。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as a positive allosteric modulator of GABA-A receptors at a binding site distinct from both benzodiazepines and barbiturates. Enhances GABAergic inhibition, producing sedative, hypnotic, anxiolytic, and muscle relaxant effects. Also has weak inhibitory effects on voltage-gated sodium channels." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为 GABA-A 受体的正向变构调节剂,结合位点与苯二氮䓬类和巴比妥类均不同。增强 GABA 能抑制,产生镇静、催眠、抗焦虑和肌肉松弛作用。对电压门控钠通道也有微弱抑制作用。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為 GABA-A 受體的正向變構調節劑,結合位點與苯二氮䓬類和巴比妥類均不同。增強 GABA 能抑制,產生鎮靜、催眠、抗焦慮和肌肉鬆弛作用。對電壓門控鈉通道也有微弱抑制作用。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as a potent agonist at both serotonin 5-HT1A and 5-HT2A receptors. The strong 5-HT1A activation distinguishes it from most classical psychedelics and contributes to its characteristic intense, ego-dissolving effects with less visual distortion. Like DMT, rapidly metabolized by MAO. The 5-HT1A component may produce cardiovascular effects including hypotension." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为血清素 5-HT1A 和 5-HT2A 受体的强效激动剂。强烈的 5-HT1A 激活使其有别于大多数经典致幻剂,并对其特征性的强烈、自我消融效应(视觉扭曲较少)有贡献。与 DMT 一样,迅速被 MAO 代谢。5-HT1A 成分可能产生包括低血压在内的心血管效应。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為血清素 5-HT1A 和 5-HT2A 受體的強效激動劑。強烈的 5-HT1A 激活使其有別於大多數經典致幻劑,並對其特徵性的強烈、自我消融效應(視覺扭曲較少)有貢獻。與 DMT 一樣,迅速被 MAO 代謝。5-HT1A 成分可能產生包括低血壓在內的心血管效應。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as a μ-opioid receptor agonist on myenteric plexus neurons in the gastrointestinal tract, reducing peristalsis and intestinal secretion. Does not cross the blood-brain barrier at therapeutic doses due to P-glycoprotein efflux, so it produces antidiarrheal effects without central opioid effects. At very high (supratherapeutic) doses, may overwhelm the efflux mechanism." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为胃肠道肌间神经丛神经元上的 μ-阿片受体激动剂,减少蠕动和肠分泌。由于 P-糖蛋白外排,治疗剂量下不穿过血脑屏障,因此产生止泻作用而无中枢阿片效应。在极高(超治疗)剂量下,可能压垮外排机制。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為胃腸道肌間神經叢神經元上的 μ-阿片受體激動劑,減少蠕動和腸分泌。由於 P-糖蛋白外排,治療劑量下不穿過血腦屏障,因此產生止瀉作用而無中樞阿片效應。在極高(超治療)劑量下,可能壓垮外排機制。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as an agonist at cannabinoid CB1 receptors in the central nervous system and CB2 receptors in immune tissues. CB1 activation inhibits adenylyl cyclase and modulates ion channels via Gi/Go proteins, reducing neurotransmitter release (particularly GABA and glutamate) in brain regions involved in reward, memory, coordination, and pain perception." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为中枢神经系统中大麻素 CB1 受体和免疫组织中 CB2 受体的激动剂。CB1 激活抑制腺苷酸环化酶,并通过 Gi/Go 蛋白调节离子通道,减少参与奖赏、记忆、协调和痛觉的脑区中的神经递质释放(尤其是 GABA 和谷氨酸)。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為中樞神經系統中大麻素 CB1 受體和免疫組織中 CB2 受體的激動劑。CB1 激活抑制腺苷酸環化酶,並透過 Gi/Go 蛋白調節離子通道,減少參與獎賞、記憶、協調和痛覺的腦區中的神經傳導物質釋放(尤其是 GABA 和麩胺酸)。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as an agonist at nicotinic acetylcholine receptors (nAChRs), ligand-gated ion channels that open in response to acetylcholine. Primary targets include α4β2 nAChRs (high affinity, involved in reward and cognition) and α7 nAChRs (involved in cognitive enhancement). Activation of nAChRs in the ventral tegmental area stimulates dopamine release in the nucleus accumbens, mediating reinforcing effects and addiction." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为烟碱型乙酰胆碱受体 (nAChR) 的激动剂,这些是响应乙酰胆碱开放的配体门控离子通道。主要靶点包括 α4β2 nAChR(高亲和力,参与奖赏和认知)和 α7 nAChR(参与认知增强)。腹侧被盖区 nAChR 的激活刺激伏隔核多巴胺释放,介导强化效应和成瘾。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為菸鹼型乙醯膽鹼受體 (nAChR) 的激動劑,這些是響應乙醯膽鹼開放的配體門控離子通道。主要靶點包括 α4β2 nAChR(高親和力,參與獎賞和認知)和 α7 nAChR(參與認知增強)。腹側被蓋區 nAChR 的激活刺激伏隔核多巴胺釋放,介導強化效應和成癮。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as an agonist at serotonin 5-HT2A receptors (primary psychedelic mechanism) and also activates sigma-1 receptors, which may modulate ion channels, ER stress responses, and neuroplasticity. Additionally interacts with trace amine-associated receptors. DMT is rapidly metabolized by monoamine oxidase (MAO), requiring an MAO inhibitor (as in ayahuasca) for oral activity." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为血清素 5-HT2A 受体的激动剂(主要致幻机制),并激活 sigma-1 受体,后者可能调节离子通道、内质网应激反应和神经可塑性。另外与痕量胺相关受体相互作用。DMT 被单胺氧化酶 (MAO) 快速代谢,口服需要 MAO 抑制剂(如死藤水中)。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為血清素 5-HT2A 受體的激動劑(主要致幻機制),並激活 sigma-1 受體,後者可能調節離子通道、內質網應激反應和神經可塑性。另外與痕量胺相關受體相互作用。DMT 被單胺氧化酶 (MAO) 快速代謝,口服需要 MAO 抑制劑(如死藤水中)。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as an agonist at the GHB receptor (Gi/Go-coupled) and at GABA-B receptors. At lower concentrations, GHB receptor activation modulates dopamine and glutamate release. At higher concentrations, GABA-B agonism predominates, producing sedation and anesthesia. GHB is an endogenous substance in the human brain, synthesized from GABA. Its steep dose-response curve makes it particularly dangerous." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为 GHB 受体(Gi/Go 偶联)和 GABA-B 受体的激动剂。在较低浓度下,GHB 受体激活调节多巴胺和谷氨酸释放。在较高浓度下,GABA-B 激动占主导,产生镇静和麻醉。GHB 是人脑中的内源性物质,由 GABA 合成。其陡峭的剂量-反应曲线使其特别危险。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為 GHB 受體(Gi/Go 偶聯)和 GABA-B 受體的激動劑。在較低濃度下,GHB 受體激活調節多巴胺和麩胺酸釋放。在較高濃度下,GABA-B 激動佔主導,產生鎮靜和麻醉。GHB 是人腦中的內源性物質,由 GABA 合成。其陡峭的劑量-反應曲線使其特別危險。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts as an inverse agonist at histamine H1 receptors, reducing constitutive receptor activity and blocking histamine-mediated signaling. Crosses the blood-brain barrier readily, producing sedation, anxiolysis, and antiemetic activity through central H1 blockade. Most also have significant anticholinergic (muscarinic antagonist) activity." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作为组胺 H1 受体的反向激动剂,减少受体的本征活性并阻断组胺介导的信号传导。易于穿过血脑屏障,通过中枢 H1 阻断产生镇静、抗焦虑和止吐作用。大多数还具有显著的抗胆碱(毒蕈碱拮抗)活性。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "作為組胺 H1 受體的反向激動劑,減少受體的本徵活性並阻斷組胺介導的訊號傳導。易於穿過血腦屏障,透過中樞 H1 阻斷產生鎮靜、抗焦慮和止吐作用。大多數還具有顯著的抗膽鹼(蕈毒鹼拮抗)活性。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts on multiple neurotransmitter systems simultaneously: NMDA receptor antagonist, κ-opioid receptor agonist, σ-receptor agonist, and serotonin transporter inhibitor. Also interacts with nicotinic acetylcholine receptors. Its active metabolite noribogaine has prolonged μ-opioid receptor activity. The complex pharmacological profile may reduce opioid withdrawal and craving, but carries significant cardiac risk via hERG potassium channel inhibition." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "同时作用于多种神经递质系统:NMDA 受体拮抗剂、κ-阿片受体激动剂、σ-受体激动剂和血清素转运体抑制剂。也与烟碱型乙酰胆碱受体相互作用。其活性代谢物 noribogaine 有持续的 μ-阿片受体活性。复杂的药理学谱可能减少阿片戒断和渴求,但通过 hERG 钾通道抑制带来显著的心脏风险。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "同時作用於多種神經傳導物質系統:NMDA 受體拮抗劑、κ-阿片受體激動劑、σ-受體激動劑和血清素轉運體抑制劑。也與菸鹼型乙醯膽鹼受體相互作用。其活性代謝物 noribogaine 有持續的 μ-阿片受體活性。複雜的藥理學譜可能減少阿片戒斷和渴求,但透過 hERG 鉀通道抑制帶來顯著的心臟風險。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts through multiple mechanisms: blocks voltage-gated sodium channels, enhances GABA activity at GABA-A receptors, antagonizes AMPA/kainate glutamate receptors, and inhibits carbonic anhydrase (isoenzymes II and IV). This combination of GABAergic enhancement and glutamatergic reduction provides broad-spectrum anticonvulsant activity. The carbonic anhydrase inhibition contributes to appetite suppression and metabolic acidosis." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "通过多种机制起作用:阻断电压门控钠通道,增强 GABA 在 GABA-A 受体的活性,拮抗 AMPA/红藻氨酸盐谷氨酸受体,并抑制碳酸酐酶(同工酶 II 和 IV)。GABA 能增强与谷氨酸能减少的组合提供广谱抗惊厥活性。碳酸酐酶抑制助长食欲抑制和代谢性酸中毒。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "透過多種機制起作用:阻斷電壓門控鈉通道,增強 GABA 在 GABA-A 受體的活性,拮抗 AMPA/紅藻氨酸鹽麩胺酸受體,並抑制碳酸酐酶(同工酶 II 和 IV)。GABA 能增強與麩胺酸能減少的組合提供廣譜抗驚厥活性。碳酸酐酶抑制助長食慾抑制和代謝性酸中毒。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts through multiple mechanisms: increases GABA levels by inhibiting GABA transaminase and enhancing GABA synthesis. Blocks voltage-gated sodium channels, reducing repetitive neuronal firing. Inhibits T-type calcium channels in thalamic neurons. Also inhibits histone deacetylases (HDACs), modifying gene expression, which may contribute to neuroprotective and mood-stabilizing effects." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "通过多种机制起作用:通过抑制 GABA 转氨酶和增强 GABA 合成来提高 GABA 水平。阻断电压门控钠通道,减少重复性神经元放电。抑制丘脑神经元中的 T 型钙通道。也抑制组蛋白脱乙酰酶 (HDAC),修饰基因表达,这可能对神经保护和情绪稳定效应有贡献。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "透過多種機制起作用:透過抑制 GABA 轉胺酶和增強 GABA 合成來提高 GABA 水平。阻斷電壓門控鈉通道,減少重複性神經元放電。抑制丘腦神經元中的 T 型鈣通道。也抑制組蛋白脫乙醯酶 (HDAC),修飾基因表達,這可能對神經保護和情緒穩定效應有貢獻。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acts through multiple mechanisms: increases GABA levels by inhibiting GABA transaminase and enhancing GABA synthesis. Blocks voltage-gated sodium channels, reducing repetitive neuronal firing. Inhibits T-type calcium channels in thalamic neurons. Also inhibits histone deacetylases (HDACs)." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
