    "AMPAkine" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "安帕金"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "安帕金"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An amino acid analogue of glutamate found in tea leaves. Crosses the blood-brain barrier and increases brain levels of GABA, serotonin, and dopamine. May antagonize glutamate at AMPA receptors and modulate α-wave brain activity. Promotes relaxation without sedation, and may attenuate the anxiogenic effects of caffeine when co-administered." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "茶叶中发现的谷氨酸氨基酸类似物。穿过血脑屏障,提高脑内 GABA、血清素和多巴胺水平。可能在 AMPA 受体拮抗谷氨酸,并调节 α 波脑活动。促进放松而不镇静,与咖啡因合用时可能减弱咖啡因的致焦虑效应。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "茶葉中發現的麩胺酸胺基酸類似物。穿過血腦屏障,提高腦內 GABA、血清素和多巴胺水平。可能在 AMPA 受體拮抗麩胺酸,並調節 α 波腦活動。促進放鬆而不鎮靜,與咖啡因合用時可能減弱咖啡因的致焦慮效應。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An electrolyte drink is better than plain water if available." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "如果有,电解质饮料比清水更好。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "如果有,電解質飲料比清水更好。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An endogenous intermediate in phosphatidylcholine synthesis. Provides both choline (for acetylcholine synthesis) and cytidine (converted to uridine, which supports synaptic membrane formation). Enhances dopamine receptor density and dopamine release in addition to cholinergic effects. Supports neuronal membrane integrity and repair." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "磷脂酰胆碱合成中的内源性中间体。同时提供胆碱(用于乙酰胆碱合成)和胞苷(转化为支持突触膜形成的尿苷)。除胆碱能效应外还增强多巴胺受体密度和多巴胺释放。支持神经元膜的完整性和修复。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "磷脂醯膽鹼合成中的內源性中間體。同時提供膽鹼(用於乙醯膽鹼合成)和胞苷(轉化為支持突觸膜形成的尿苷)。除膽鹼能效應外還增強多巴胺受體密度和多巴胺釋放。支持神經元膜的完整性和修復。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An N-benzylmethoxy derivative that acts as a highly potent full agonist at serotonin 5-HT2A receptors with much greater efficacy than partial agonists like LSD. The full agonism and high potency at 5-HT2A receptors are associated with a steeper dose-response curve, greater risk of seizures, vasoconstriction, and a narrower margin of safety compared to classical partial agonist psychedelics." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "N-苄基甲氧基衍生物,作为血清素 5-HT2A 受体的高效完全激动剂,效能远高于 LSD 等部分激动剂。在 5-HT2A 受体的完全激动和高效力与较陡的剂量-反应曲线、较大的癫痫发作和血管收缩风险及比经典部分激动致幻剂更窄的安全边际有关。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "N-苄基甲氧基衍生物,作為血清素 5-HT2A 受體的高效完全激動劑,效能遠高於 LSD 等部分激動劑。在 5-HT2A 受體的完全激動和高效力與較陡的劑量-反應曲線、較大的癲癇發作和血管收縮風險及比經典部分激動致幻劑更窄的安全邊際有關。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "An N-benzylmethoxy phenethylamine that acts as a full agonist at 5-HT2A receptors with very high potency. Like other NBOMe compounds, the full agonism contributes to a steeper dose-response curve and greater toxicity risk compared to classical psychedelics. Active at microgram doses." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "N-苄基甲氧基苯乙胺,作为 5-HT2A 受体的完全激动剂,效力极高。与其他 NBOMe 化合物一样,完全激动比经典致幻剂带来更陡的剂量-反应曲线和更大的毒性风险。在微克剂量下即有效。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "N-苄基甲氧基苯乙胺,作為 5-HT2A 受體的完全激動劑,效力極高。與其他 NBOMe 化合物一樣,完全激動比經典致幻劑帶來更陡的劑量-反應曲線和更大的毒性風險。在微克劑量下即有效。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
