        }
      }
    },
    "Colors appear here after you log your first entry. Tap one to change it." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "记录第一条条目后，配色会显示在这里。点按即可更改。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "記錄第一筆項目後，配色會顯示在這裡。點按即可更改。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Combine repeat doses of the same substance into a single curve, where each redose adds to the combined intensity. When off, each dose is drawn as its own line." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "将同一物质的重复剂量合并为单条曲线,每次重复剂量都会加到综合强度中。关闭时,每个剂量都会作为独立线条绘制。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "將同一物質的重複劑量合併為單條曲線,每次重複劑量都會加到綜合強度中。關閉時,每個劑量都會作為獨立線條繪製。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Combined QTc prolongation risk — monitor cardiac rhythm." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "联合 QTc 延长的风险 — 监测心律。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "聯合 QTc 延長的風險 — 監測心律。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Combined respiratory depression — the leading cause of overdose death." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "联合呼吸抑制 — 过量致死的首要原因。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "聯合呼吸抑制 — 過量致死的首要原因。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Combines serotonin 5-HT2A receptor antagonism with serotonin reuptake inhibition (SERT blockade). The 5-HT2A antagonism occurs at lower doses, producing anxiolytic and sleep-promoting effects. At higher antidepressant doses, SERT inhibition enhances serotonergic neurotransmission. Also blocks α1-adrenergic receptors and histamine H1 receptors, contributing to sedation." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "将血清素 5-HT2A 受体拮抗与血清素再摄取抑制 (SERT 阻断) 相结合。5-HT2A 拮抗在较低剂量下发生,产生抗焦虑和促进睡眠的效应。在较高抗抑郁剂量下,SERT 抑制增强血清素能神经传递。也阻断 α1-肾上腺素受体和组胺 H1 受体,助长镇静效应。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "將血清素 5-HT2A 受體拮抗與血清素再攝取抑制 (SERT 阻斷) 相結合。5-HT2A 拮抗在較低劑量下發生,產生抗焦慮和促進睡眠的效應。在較高抗鬱劑量下,SERT 抑制增強血清素能神經傳導。也阻斷 α1-腎上腺素受體和組胺 H1 受體,助長鎮靜效應。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Combines serotonin reuptake inhibition (SERT blockade) with partial agonism at serotonin 5-HT1A receptors. The 5-HT1A partial agonism may accelerate the onset of antidepressant action by partially bypassing the delayed desensitization of presynaptic autoreceptors required by pure SSRIs. May produce fewer sexual side effects than SSRIs due to 5-HT1A activity." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "将血清素再摄取抑制 (SERT 阻断) 与血清素 5-HT1A 受体的部分激动作用相结合。5-HT1A 部分激动可能通过部分绕过纯 SSRI 所需的突触前自身受体延迟去敏化,加速抗抑郁作用的起效。由于 5-HT1A 活性,可能比 SSRI 产生更少的性副作用。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "將血清素再攝取抑制 (SERT 阻斷) 與血清素 5-HT1A 受體的部分激動作用相結合。5-HT1A 部分激動可能透過部分繞過純 SSRI 所需的突觸前自身受體延遲去敏化,加速抗鬱作用的起效。由於 5-HT1A 活性,可能比 SSRI 產生更少的性副作用。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Combines SERT inhibition with direct modulation of multiple serotonin receptors: agonist at 5-HT1A, partial agonist at 5-HT1B, antagonist at 5-HT1D, 5-HT3, and 5-HT7 receptors. This multimodal mechanism enhances downstream release of serotonin, norepinephrine, dopamine, histamine, and acetylcholine. The 5-HT3 and 5-HT7 antagonism may contribute to procognitive effects." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "将 SERT 抑制与对多种血清素受体的直接调节相结合:5-HT1A 激动剂、5-HT1B 部分激动剂、5-HT1D、5-HT3 和 5-HT7 受体拮抗剂。这种多模式机制增强下游血清素、去甲肾上腺素、多巴胺、组胺和乙酰胆碱的释放。5-HT3 和 5-HT7 拮抗作用可能对促认知效应有贡献。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "將 SERT 抑制與對多種血清素受體的直接調節相結合:5-HT1A 激動劑、5-HT1B 部分激動劑、5-HT1D、5-HT3 和 5-HT7 受體拮抗劑。這種多模式機制增強下游血清素、去甲腎上腺素、多巴胺、組胺和乙醯膽鹼的釋放。5-HT3 和 5-HT7 拮抗作用可能對促認知效應有貢獻。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Combines μ-opioid receptor (MOR) agonism with norepinephrine reuptake inhibition (NET blockade) in a single molecule. Unlike tramadol, tapentadol does not require metabolic activation and does not significantly affect serotonin. The dual mechanism provides synergistic analgesia with a lower opioid burden and reduced gastrointestinal side effects compared to equianalgesic doses of classical opioids." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "在单一分子中结合 μ-阿片受体 (MOR) 激动作用与去甲肾上腺素再摄取抑制 (NET 阻断)。与曲马多不同,他喷他多不需要代谢激活,也不显著影响血清素。这种双重机制提供协同镇痛,与等镇痛剂量的经典阿片相比,阿片负担较低,胃肠道副作用减少。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "在單一分子中結合 μ-阿片受體 (MOR) 激動作用與去甲腎上腺素再攝取抑制 (NET 阻斷)。與曲馬多不同,他噴他多不需要代謝激活,也不顯著影響血清素。這種雙重機制提供協同鎮痛,與等鎮痛劑量的經典阿片相比,阿片負擔較低,胃腸道副作用減少。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Come-up" : {
      "localizations" : {
