            "value" : "請輸入有效的 6 位十六進位顏色代碼"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Enter a vial amount, diluent volume, and target dose." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "请输入瓶内总量、溶剂体积和目标剂量。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "請輸入瓶內總量、溶劑體積與目標劑量。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Enter Passphrase" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "输入口令"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "輸入通行碼"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Enters monoaminergic nerve terminals via dopamine (DAT), norepinephrine (NET), and serotonin (SERT) transporters, then reverses their function to release stored neurotransmitters into the synaptic cleft. Also activates trace amine-associated receptor 1 (TAAR1), inhibits vesicular monoamine transporter 2 (VMAT2), and weakly inhibits monoamine oxidase. The net effect is a substantial increase in synaptic dopamine, norepinephrine, and to a lesser extent serotonin." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "通过多巴胺 (DAT)、去甲肾上腺素 (NET) 和血清素 (SERT) 转运体进入单胺能神经末梢,然后反转它们的功能,将储存的神经递质释放到突触间隙。也激活痕量胺相关受体 1 (TAAR1),抑制囊泡单胺转运体 2 (VMAT2),并弱抑制单胺氧化酶。净效应是突触多巴胺、去甲肾上腺素的大幅增加,以及较小程度的血清素增加。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "透過多巴胺 (DAT)、去甲腎上腺素 (NET) 和血清素 (SERT) 轉運體進入單胺能神經末梢,然後反轉它們的功能,將儲存的神經傳導物質釋放到突觸間隙。也激活痕量胺相關受體 1 (TAAR1),抑制囊泡單胺轉運體 2 (VMAT2),並弱抑制單胺氧化酶。淨效應是突觸多巴胺、去甲腎上腺素的大幅增加,以及較小程度的血清素增加。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Enters serotonergic, dopaminergic, and noradrenergic nerve terminals via their respective transporters and reverses transporter function to release stored monoamines. Has strongest affinity for SERT, producing pronounced serotonin release that distinguishes it from amphetamine. Also stimulates oxytocin release from the hypothalamus, contributing to prosocial and empathogenic effects. Additionally directly inhibits SERT, DAT, and NET reuptake." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "通过各自的转运体进入血清素能、多巴胺能和去甲肾上腺素能神经末梢,反转转运体功能以释放储存的单胺。对 SERT 亲和力最强,产生显著的血清素释放,这是其与苯丙胺的区别。也刺激下丘脑释放催产素,助长亲社会和共感效应。另外直接抑制 SERT、DAT 和 NET 的再摄取。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "透過各自的轉運體進入血清素能、多巴胺能和去甲腎上腺素能神經末梢,反轉轉運體功能以釋放儲存的單胺。對 SERT 親和力最強,產生顯著的血清素釋放,這是其與苯丙胺的區別。也刺激下丘腦釋放催產素,助長親社會和共感效應。另外直接抑制 SERT、DAT 和 NET 的再攝取。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Entries" : {
      "localizations" : {
