        }
      }
    },
    "Increased anxiety and vasoconstriction — stimulants can intensify difficult trips." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "焦虑加剧和血管收缩 — 兴奋剂会加重艰难的体验。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "焦慮加劇和血管收縮 — 興奮劑會加重艱難的體驗。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Increased heart rate and blood pressure — cardiovascular strain." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "心率和血压增加 — 心血管压力。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "心率和血壓增加 — 心血管壓力。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Increased risk of serotonin syndrome and lithium toxicity." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "血清素综合征和锂中毒的风险增加。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "血清素綜合徵和鋰中毒的風險增加。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Increases central nervous system activity by enhancing monoamine neurotransmission, typically through increased release or reduced reuptake of dopamine and/or norepinephrine. The specific mechanism varies by substance class (releasing agents, reuptake inhibitors, or receptor agonists). Effects include increased alertness, attention, and energy." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "通过增强单胺神经传递增加中枢神经系统活性,通常通过增加释放或减少多巴胺和/或去甲肾上腺素的再摄取。具体机制因物质类别(释放剂、再摄取抑制剂或受体激动剂)而异。效应包括警觉度、注意力和能量增加。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "透過增強單胺神經傳導增加中樞神經系統活性,通常透過增加釋放或減少多巴胺和/或去甲腎上腺素的再攝取。具體機制因物質類別(釋放劑、再攝取抑制劑或受體激動劑)而異。效應包括警覺度、注意力和能量增加。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Increases synaptic serotonin, dopamine, and norepinephrine, with a predominant serotonergic component that distinguishes empathogens from classical stimulants. Many also stimulate the release of oxytocin from the hypothalamus, contributing to prosocial effects, emotional openness, and feelings of empathy and connectedness." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "增加突触血清素、多巴胺和去甲肾上腺素,以血清素能成分为主,这使共感剂与经典兴奋剂相区别。许多还刺激下丘脑释放催产素,助长亲社会效应、情感开放及共情和连结感。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "增加突觸血清素、多巴胺和去甲腎上腺素,以血清素能成分為主,這使共感劑與經典興奮劑相區別。許多還刺激下丘腦釋放催產素,助長親社會效應、情感開放及共情和連結感。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Info" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "信息"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "資訊"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ingestion time" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "摄入时间"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "攝入時間"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Inhalation" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "吸入"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "吸入"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Inhalers, decongestants, and cough." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "吸入剂、减充血剂与止咳药。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "吸入劑、減充血劑與止咳藥。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Inhibits angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE), preventing the conversion of angiotensin I to angiotensin II, a potent vasoconstrictor. Also reduces degradation of bradykinin, a vasodilator. The net effect is decreased peripheral vascular resistance, reduced aldosterone secretion, and lower blood pressure. ACE inhibitors also reduce cardiac remodeling after myocardial infarction." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "抑制血管紧张素转换酶 (ACE),阻止血管紧张素 I 转化为强效血管收缩剂血管紧张素 II。也减少血管扩张剂缓激肽的降解。净效应是外周血管阻力降低、醛固酮分泌减少和血压降低。ACE 抑制剂也减少心肌梗死后的心脏重塑。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "抑制血管收縮素轉換酶 (ACE),阻止血管收縮素 I 轉化為強效血管收縮劑血管收縮素 II。也減少血管擴張劑緩激肽的降解。淨效應是外周血管阻力降低、醛固酮分泌減少和血壓降低。ACE 抑制劑也減少心肌梗塞後的心臟重塑。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Inhibits bacterial DNA gyrase (topoisomerase II) and topoisomerase IV, enzymes essential for DNA replication, transcription, repair, and recombination. DNA gyrase inhibition prevents supercoil relaxation; topoisomerase IV inhibition prevents daughter chromosome separation. These actions are bactericidal. Human topoisomerases are structurally different, providing selectivity." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "抑制细菌 DNA 旋转酶(拓扑异构酶 II)和拓扑异构酶 IV,这是 DNA 复制、转录、修复和重组所必需的酶。DNA 旋转酶抑制阻止超螺旋松弛;拓扑异构酶 IV 抑制阻止子代染色体分离。这些作用是杀菌性的。人类拓扑异构酶结构不同,提供选择性。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "抑制細菌 DNA 旋轉酶(拓樸異構酶 II)和拓樸異構酶 IV,這是 DNA 複製、轉錄、修復和重組所必需的酶。DNA 旋轉酶抑制阻止超螺旋鬆弛;拓樸異構酶 IV 抑制阻止子代染色體分離。這些作用是殺菌性的。人類拓樸異構酶結構不同,提供選擇性。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Inhibits both the serotonin transporter (SERT) and the norepinephrine transporter (NET), blocking reuptake of both monoamines from the synaptic cleft. At lower doses, serotonin reuptake inhibition predominates; norepinephrine reuptake inhibition becomes more significant at higher doses. This dual mechanism provides antidepressant and analgesic effects." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "抑制血清素转运体 (SERT) 和去甲肾上腺素转运体 (NET),阻断这两种单胺从突触间隙的再摄取。低剂量下血清素再摄取抑制占主导;高剂量下去甲肾上腺素再摄取抑制更显著。这种双重机制提供抗抑郁和镇痛效应。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "抑制血清素轉運體 (SERT) 和去甲腎上腺素轉運體 (NET),阻斷這兩種單胺從突觸間隙的再攝取。低劑量下血清素再攝取抑制佔主導;高劑量下去甲腎上腺素再攝取抑制更顯著。這種雙重機制提供抗鬱和鎮痛效應。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Inhibits the reuptake of norepinephrine (NET) and dopamine (DAT), increasing their synaptic availability. Unlike most antidepressants, has minimal effect on serotonin and does not cause sexual dysfunction or weight gain. Also acts as a non-competitive antagonist at nicotinic acetylcholine receptors, contributing to its efficacy in smoking cessation. Its active metabolite hydroxybupropion has a longer half-life and contributes significantly to clinical effects." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "抑制去甲肾上腺素 (NET) 和多巴胺 (DAT) 的再摄取,增加它们的突触可用性。与大多数抗抑郁药不同,对血清素影响极小,不引起性功能障碍或体重增加。也作为烟碱型乙酰胆碱受体的非竞争性拮抗剂,助长其戒烟疗效。其活性代谢物羟基安非他酮半衰期较长,对临床效应有显著贡献。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "抑制去甲腎上腺素 (NET) 和多巴胺 (DAT) 的再攝取,增加它們的突觸可用性。與大多數抗鬱藥不同,對血清素影響極小,不引起性功能障礙或體重增加。也作為菸鹼型乙醯膽鹼受體的非競爭性拮抗劑,助長其戒菸療效。其活性代謝物羥基安非他酮半衰期較長,對臨床效應有顯著貢獻。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Inhibits the reuptake of serotonin and norepinephrine by blocking SERT and NET. Unlike SSRIs and SNRIs, TCAs also significantly antagonize histamine H1, muscarinic M1, and α1-adrenergic receptors, which accounts for their sedative, anticholinergic, and orthostatic hypotension side effects. The ratio of serotonin to norepinephrine reuptake inhibition varies between individual TCAs." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "通过阻断 SERT 和 NET 抑制血清素和去甲肾上腺素的再摄取。与 SSRI 和 SNRI 不同,TCA 还显著拮抗组胺 H1、毒蕈碱 M1 和 α1-肾上腺素受体,这解释了其镇静、抗胆碱和直立性低血压副作用。各 TCA 之间血清素与去甲肾上腺素再摄取抑制的比例各不相同。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "透過阻斷 SERT 和 NET 抑制血清素和去甲腎上腺素的再攝取。與 SSRI 和 SNRI 不同,TCA 還顯著拮抗組胺 H1、蕈毒鹼 M1 和 α1-腎上腺素受體,這解釋了其鎮靜、抗膽鹼和直立性低血壓副作用。各 TCA 之間血清素與去甲腎上腺素再攝取抑制的比例各不相同。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Inhibits vitamin K epoxide reductase (VKORC1), preventing the recycling of vitamin K to its active reduced form. Vitamin K is essential for the post-translational carboxylation of clotting factors II, VII, IX, and X, as well as proteins C and S. Onset of anticoagulant effect is delayed (3–5 days) until existing clotting factors are cleared." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "抑制维生素 K 环氧化物还原酶 (VKORC1),阻止维生素 K 循环至其活性还原形式。维生素 K 对凝血因子 II、VII、IX 和 X 以及蛋白 C 和 S 的翻译后羧化至关重要。抗凝效应的起效延迟 (3–5 天),直到现有凝血因子被清除。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "抑制維生素 K 環氧化物還原酶 (VKORC1),阻止維生素 K 循環至其活性還原形式。維生素 K 對凝血因子 II、VII、IX 和 X 以及蛋白 C 和 S 的轉譯後羧化至關重要。抗凝效應的起效延遲 (3–5 天),直到現有凝血因子被清除。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Initially classified as a serotonin reuptake enhancer, but now understood to primarily act as a full agonist at μ-opioid receptors (MOR) and δ-opioid receptors. MOR activation in the mesolimbic system produces antidepressant, anxiolytic, and analgesic effects. Also modulates glutamatergic neurotransmission and neuroplasticity in the hippocampus and amygdala." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "最初被分类为血清素再摄取增强剂,但现在被理解为主要作为 μ-阿片受体 (MOR) 和 δ-阿片受体的完全激动剂。中脑边缘系统中的 MOR 激活产生抗抑郁、抗焦虑和镇痛效应。也调节海马和杏仁核中的谷氨酸能神经传递和神经可塑性。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "最初被分類為血清素再攝取增強劑,但現在被理解為主要作為 μ-阿片受體 (MOR) 和 δ-阿片受體的完全激動劑。中腦邊緣系統中的 MOR 激活產生抗鬱、抗焦慮和鎮痛效應。也調節海馬和杏仁核中的麩胺酸能神經傳導和神經可塑性。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
