          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The active compound salvinorin A is a structurally unique non-nitrogenous terpenoid that acts as a highly potent and selective agonist at κ-opioid receptors (KOR). Unlike virtually all other known psychoactive compounds, it has no significant activity at serotonin 5-HT2A receptors. KOR activation in the claustrum and prefrontal cortex produces intensely dissociative and hallucinatory effects." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "活性化合物鼠尾草素 A 是一种结构独特的非氮萜类化合物,作为高效且选择性的 κ-阿片受体 (KOR) 激动剂。与几乎所有其他已知精神活性化合物不同,对血清素 5-HT2A 受体无显著活性。屏状核和前额叶皮质中的 KOR 激活产生强烈的解离和致幻效应。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "活性化合物鼠尾草素 A 是一種結構獨特的非氮萜類化合物,作為高效且選擇性的 κ-阿片受體 (KOR) 激動劑。與幾乎所有其他已知精神活性化合物不同,對血清素 5-HT2A 受體無顯著活性。屏狀核和前額葉皮質中的 KOR 激活產生強烈的解離和致幻效應。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The crash is your nervous system demanding rest and replenishment." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "这次崩溃是您的神经系统在要求休息和补充。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "這次崩潰是您的神經系統在要求休息和補充。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The databases and primary literature behind this compound's data. Tap to open; always verify against the original source." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "本化合物数据背后的数据库与原始文献。点按打开；请始终对照原始来源核实。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "本化合物資料背後的資料庫與原始文獻。點按開啟；請始終對照原始來源核實。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The discomfort peaks and then fades. Give it time." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "不适会达到顶峰然后消退。给它时间。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "不適會達到頂峰然後消退。給它時間。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The foggy feeling will clear. Give it hours, not minutes." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "迷糊感会消散。需要数小时,而非数分钟。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "迷糊感會消散。需要數小時,而非數分鐘。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The immediate biosynthetic precursor to serotonin (5-HT). Crosses the blood-brain barrier and is converted to serotonin by aromatic L-amino acid decarboxylase (AADC). Unlike tryptophan, bypasses the rate-limiting tryptophan hydroxylase step. Increases central serotonin synthesis. Should not be combined with serotonergic medications due to serotonin syndrome risk." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "血清素 (5-HT) 的直接生物合成前体。穿过血脑屏障,由芳香族 L-氨基酸脱羧酶 (AADC) 转化为血清素。与色氨酸不同,绕过限速的色氨酸羟化酶步骤。增加中枢血清素合成。由于血清素综合征风险,不应与血清素能药物合用。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "血清素 (5-HT) 的直接生物合成前體。穿過血腦屏障,由芳香族 L-胺基酸脫羧酶 (AADC) 轉化為血清素。與色胺酸不同,繞過限速的色胺酸羥化酶步驟。增加中樞血清素合成。由於血清素綜合徵風險,不應與血清素能藥物合用。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The low mood is chemical, not a reflection of reality. It lifts." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "情绪低落源于化学变化,并非现实的反映。它会过去。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "情緒低落源於化學變化,並非現實的反映。它會過去。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The low mood is temporary and normal. Eat light foods, stay warm, and rest. Be kind to yourself over the next few days." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "情绪低落是暂时且正常的。吃清淡食物、保暖、休息。接下来几天善待自己。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "情緒低落是暫時且正常的。吃清淡食物、保暖、休息。接下來幾天善待自己。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The primary alkaloid in kratom. Acts as a partial agonist at μ-opioid receptors (MOR), producing dose-dependent analgesic and euphoric effects. At lower doses, stimulant-like effects are attributed to α2-adrenergic agonism and 5-HT2A antagonism. The metabolite 7-hydroxymitragynine has significantly higher MOR potency. Also acts as a κ-opioid receptor antagonist." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "克拉通中的主要生物碱。作为 μ-阿片受体 (MOR) 的部分激动剂,产生剂量依赖的镇痛和欣快效应。在较低剂量下,类兴奋剂效应归因于 α2-肾上腺素激动和 5-HT2A 拮抗。代谢物 7-羟基米屈格宁的 MOR 效力显著更高。也作为 κ-阿片受体拮抗剂。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "克拉通中的主要生物鹼。作為 μ-阿片受體 (MOR) 的部分激動劑,產生劑量依賴的鎮痛和欣快效應。在較低劑量下,類興奮劑效應歸因於 α2-腎上腺素激動和 5-HT2A 拮抗。代謝物 7-羥基米屈格寧的 MOR 效力顯著更高。也作為 κ-阿片受體拮抗劑。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The primary alkaloid mitragynine acts as a partial agonist at μ-opioid receptors (MOR), producing dose-dependent analgesic and euphoric effects. At lower doses, stimulant-like effects are attributed to α2-adrenergic agonism and 5-HT2A antagonism. The metabolite 7-hydroxymitragynine has significantly higher MOR potency. Unlike classical opioids, mitragynine also acts as a κ-opioid receptor antagonist." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "主要生物碱米屈格宁作为 μ-阿片受体 (MOR) 的部分激动剂,产生剂量依赖的镇痛和欣快效应。在较低剂量下,类兴奋剂效应归因于 α2-肾上腺素激动和 5-HT2A 拮抗。代谢物 7-羟基米屈格宁的 MOR 效力显著更高。与经典阿片不同,米屈格宁也作为 κ-阿片受体拮抗剂。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "主要生物鹼米屈格寧作為 μ-阿片受體 (MOR) 的部分激動劑,產生劑量依賴的鎮痛和欣快效應。在較低劑量下,類興奮劑效應歸因於 α2-腎上腺素激動和 5-HT2A 拮抗。代謝物 7-羥基米屈格寧的 MOR 效力顯著更高。與經典阿片不同,米屈格寧也作為 κ-阿片受體拮抗劑。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The protocol below reflects community or investigational use, not validated human dosing or medical advice. Many of these compounds are WADA-prohibited and lack human safety data." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "下方方案反映社区或试验性用途，并非经过验证的人体剂量或医疗建议。其中许多化合物被 WADA 禁用，且缺乏人体安全数据。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "下方方案反映社群或試驗性用途，並非經過驗證的人體劑量或醫療建議。其中許多化合物被 WADA 禁用，且缺乏人體安全數據。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The R-enantiomer of modafinil with the same mechanism: weak DAT inhibition, orexin/hypocretin neuron activation, and histamine release promotion. Has a longer effective half-life than racemic modafinil, providing more sustained wakefulness-promoting effects throughout the day." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "莫达非尼的 R-对映体,机制相同:弱 DAT 抑制、促醒素/食欲素神经元激活,以及组胺释放促进。有效半衰期比外消旋莫达非尼更长,全天提供更持续的促醒效应。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "莫達非尼的 R-對映體,機制相同:弱 DAT 抑制、促醒素/食慾素神經元激活,以及組胺釋放促進。有效半衰期比消旋莫達非尼更長,全天提供更持續的促醒效應。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "These effects are proportional to how much and how often you've been using." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "这些影响与您使用的剂量和频率成正比。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "這些影響與您使用的劑量和頻率成正比。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "These notes will appear at the end of the PDF report." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "这些备注将出现在 PDF 报告末尾。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "這些備註將出現在 PDF 報告末尾。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "This backup uses a newer format (v%lld) than this version of Piru understands. Please update the app." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "此备份使用的格式（v%lld）比当前 Piru 版本更新。请更新应用。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "此備份使用的格式（v%lld）比目前 Piru 版本更新。請更新 App。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "This calculator uses a one-compartment oral pharmacokinetic model with absorption and elimination phases. Absorption rates are estimated from known duration profiles (onset + comeup timing) when available, or use a default 4× elimination rate ratio. Population-average elimination half-lives are sourced from FDA-approved prescribing information, published pharmacokinetic studies (PubMed), and DrugBank. Half-lives for some research chemicals and novel substances are estimated from structurally similar compounds and may be less reliable.\n\nReal pharmacokinetics vary significantly based on individual metabolism, genetics, liver and kidney function, body composition, age, drug interactions, tolerance, and route of administration. Multi-compartment distribution, protein binding, active metabolites, and enterohepatic recirculation are not accounted for. Polydrug use may alter elimination rates unpredictably.\n\nThese figures are approximate population averages — not a substitute for clinical monitoring or professional medical advice. Always consult a qualified healthcare professional." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "此计算器使用一房室口服药代动力学模型,包含吸收和消除两个阶段。如有已知的持续时间数据(起效 + 上升期),则吸收速率会由此估算;否则使用默认的 4× 消除速率比。群体平均消除半衰期来源于 FDA 批准的处方信息、已发表的药代动力学研究(PubMed)以及 DrugBank。部分研究化学品和新型物质的半衰期是根据结构类似的化合物估算的,可能不够可靠。\n\n实际药代动力学因个人代谢、遗传、肝肾功能、体成分、年龄、药物相互作用、耐受性和给药途径而显著不同。多房室分布、蛋白结合、活性代谢物和肠肝循环未被纳入考虑。多药联用可能不可预测地改变消除速率。\n\n这些数字是群体的近似平均值 — 不能替代临床监测或专业医疗建议。请始终咨询合格的医疗专业人员。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "此計算器使用一房室口服藥動學模型,包含吸收和消除兩個階段。如有已知的持續時間資料(起效 + 上升期),則吸收速率會由此估算;否則使用預設的 4× 消除速率比。族群平均消除半衰期來源於 FDA 批准的處方資訊、已發表的藥動學研究(PubMed)以及 DrugBank。部分研究化學品和新型物質的半衰期是根據結構類似的化合物估算的,可能不夠可靠。\n\n實際藥動學因個人代謝、遺傳、肝腎功能、體成分、年齡、藥物相互作用、耐受性和給藥途徑而顯著不同。多房室分布、蛋白質結合、活性代謝物和腸肝循環未被納入考慮。多藥聯用可能不可預測地改變消除速率。\n\n這些數字是族群的近似平均值 — 不能替代臨床監測或專業醫療建議。請始終諮詢合格的醫療專業人員。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "This calculator uses a one-compartment oral pharmacokinetic model with absorption and elimination phases. Absorption rates are estimated from known duration profiles (onset + comeup timing) when available, or use a default 4× elimination rate ratio. Population-average elimination half-lives are sourced from FDA-approved prescribing information, published pharmacokinetic studies (PubMed), DrugBank, and established pharmacology references (Goodman & Gilman's, Stahl's Essential Psychopharmacology). Half-lives for some research chemicals and novel substances are estimated from structurally similar compounds and may be less reliable.\n\nReal pharmacokinetics vary significantly based on individual metabolism, genetics, liver and kidney function, body composition, age, drug interactions, tolerance, and route of administration. Multi-compartment distribution, protein binding, active metabolites, and enterohepatic recirculation are not accounted for. Polydrug use may alter elimination rates unpredictably.\n\nThese figures are approximate population averages — not a substitute for clinical monitoring or professional medical advice. Always consult a qualified healthcare professional." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "此计算器使用一房室口服药代动力学模型,包含吸收和消除两个阶段。如有已知的持续时间数据(起效 + 上升期),则吸收速率会由此估算;否则使用默认的 4× 消除速率比。群体平均消除半衰期来源于 FDA 批准的处方信息、已发表的药代动力学研究(PubMed)、DrugBank 以及成熟的药理学参考资料(《古德曼&吉尔曼治疗学的药理学基础》、《Stahl 精神药理学精要》)。部分研究化学品和新型物质的半衰期是根据结构类似的化合物估算的,可能不够可靠。\n\n实际药代动力学因个人代谢、遗传、肝肾功能、体成分、年龄、药物相互作用、耐受性和给药途径而显著不同。多房室分布、蛋白结合、活性代谢物和肠肝循环未被纳入考虑。多药联用可能不可预测地改变消除速率。\n\n这些数字是群体的近似平均值 — 不能替代临床监测或专业医疗建议。请始终咨询合格的医疗专业人员。"
          }
        },
        "zh-Hant" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "此計算器使用一房室口服藥動學模型,包含吸收和消除兩個階段。如有已知的持續時間資料(起效 + 上升期),則吸收速率會由此估算;否則使用預設的 4× 消除速率比。族群平均消除半衰期來源於 FDA 批准的處方資訊、已發表的藥動學研究(PubMed)、DrugBank 以及成熟的藥理學參考資料(《古德曼&吉爾曼治療學的藥理學基礎》、《Stahl 精神藥理學精要》)。部分研究化學品和新型物質的半衰期是根據結構類似的化合物估算的,可能不夠可靠。\n\n實際藥動學因個人代謝、遺傳、肝腎功能、體成分、年齡、藥物相互作用、耐受性和給藥途徑而顯著不同。多房室分布、蛋白質結合、活性代謝物和腸肝循環未被納入考慮。多藥聯用可能不可預測地改變消除速率。\n\n這些數字是族群的近似平均值 — 不能替代臨床監測或專業醫療建議。請始終諮詢合格的醫療專業人員。"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "This class isn’t in the library anymore." : {
      "extractionState" : "stale",
      "localizations" : {
        "zh-Hans" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
